%S A400879 1,2,7,22,55,121,214,475,970,2122,4316,8876,16443,36281,72909,162536,
%T A400879 321419,656225,1198005,2634534,5243230,11497714,22571793,47110953,
%U A400879 86046455,186702111,364554584,799401460
%N A400879 Number of n X n binary Riordan matrices that are poset matrices (labeled Riordan posets with n elements).
%C A400879 A binary Riordan matrix {g,f}_n has entries [t^i] g(t)*f(t)^j mod 2, 0 <= i,j < n, where g = 1 + g_1*t + ... and f = t + f_2*t^2 + ... are power series over GF(2). It is lower triangular with unit diagonal, and it is a poset matrix when it is transitive: a(i,j) = a(j,k) = 1 implies a(i,k) = 1. Such a matrix is the poset matrix of a Riordan poset under one labeling of its elements.
%C A400879 A Riordan poset may admit several labelings that give different Riordan poset matrices, so a(n) >= A379608(n), which counts the Riordan posets up to isomorphism. Every such matrix is the matrix of a naturally labeled poset, so a(n) <= A006455(n).
%C A400879 The matrix {g,f}_n determines g and f modulo t^n, so there are 2^(2n-3) binary Riordan matrices of order n >= 2, of which a(n) are poset matrices.
%H A400879 G. S. Cheon, B. Curtis, G. Kwon and A. Mesinga Mwafise, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2021.10.002">Riordan posets and associated incidence matrices</a>, Linear Algebra and its Applications, 632 (2022), 308-331.
%H A400879 Arnauld Mesinga Mwafise, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23188305">riordan-poset-enumeration: construction, enumeration and analysis of Riordan posets</a>, software, Zenodo (2026).
%e A400879 a(3) = 7: of the 2^3 = 8 binary Riordan matrices of order 3, all except {1+t, t}_3, with rows 100 / 110 / 011, are poset matrices; in that matrix a(2,1) = a(1,0) = 1 but a(2,0) = 0.
%e A400879 a(4) = 22: these 22 matrices represent the 11 Riordan posets with 4 elements (A379608(4) = 11); for example, the poset N has 5 different Riordan poset matrices, and the 4-element chain has 1.
%Y A400879 Cf. A379608, A006455, A000112.
%K A400879 nonn,more
%O A400879 1,2
